<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Codecov: Generate AI prompts from coverage" id="Codecov-AI-Prompts">

    <primary-label ref="codecov"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Generate: click a coverage bar, then <control>Generate AI Prompt</control></p>
        <p>Templates: <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>, group <control>AI Prompt Templates</control></p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Copy a test-writing prompt for covered or uncovered code to the clipboard and customize the prompt templates.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Copy a ready-made test-writing prompt for uncovered code to the clipboard.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>The Codecov plugin for JetBrains IDEs turns covered or uncovered code into a test-writing prompt that you paste into any AI assistant or agent.</web-summary>

    <p>
        From the coverage gutter, the plugin builds a prompt that contains the code of a line and copies it to the clipboard.
        Paste the prompt into the AI chat or coding agent you use.
        The plugin does not send the code to an AI service itself.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Generate a prompt" id="generate-ai-prompt">
        <procedure title="Copy a prompt for a line" id="copy-ai-prompt">
            <step>
                In the editor, click the coverage bar next to a line.
            </step>
            <step>
                In the popup, click <control>Generate AI Prompt</control>.
                A notification confirms that the prompt is on the clipboard, for example "AI prompt for uncovered code copied to clipboard!".
                <!-- planned-image src="codecov_ai_prompt_copied.png" alt="Notification confirming the AI prompt was copied to the clipboard" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Paste the prompt into your AI assistant and review the tests it suggests.
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="What the prompt contains" id="prompt-content">
        <p>The plugin picks the template and the code by the coverage status of the line you clicked:</p>
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="Covered line" id="prompt-covered">
                The <control>Prompt for covered code</control> template, with the text of that line.
            </def>
            <def title="Partially covered or not covered line" id="prompt-uncovered">
                The <control>Prompt for uncovered code</control> template, with the whole method or function when it contains the block of missed lines around the line.
                Otherwise, the prompt contains only that block of missed lines.
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Customize the prompt templates" id="customize-templates">
        <procedure title="Edit a template" id="edit-ai-prompt-template">
            <step>
                Press <shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut> (macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>) and go to <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>.
            </step>
            <step>
                In the <control>AI Prompt Templates</control> group, expand <control>Prompt Templates</control>.
                <!-- planned-image src="codecov_settings_ai_prompts.png" alt="AI Prompt Templates settings with the covered and uncovered prompt templates" -->
            </step>
            <step>
                Edit <control>Prompt for covered code</control> or <control>Prompt for uncovered code</control>.
                Keep the <code>&lt;CODE_TOKEN&gt;</code> placeholder where the code goes.
            </step>
            <step>
                Click <control>OK</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>The default template for uncovered code is:</p>
        <code-block lang="plain text">
Write comprehensive unit tests for the following code that tests do not cover:

&lt;CODE_TOKEN&gt;

Include edge cases and error scenarios. Use the project's existing test framework and follow the established testing patterns.
        </code-block>
        <p>The default template for covered code is:</p>
        <code-block lang="plain text">
Analyze the following code already covered by tests:

&lt;CODE_TOKEN&gt;

Suggest potential improvements or edge cases that could be tested.
        </code-block>
        <p>The templates are saved per project.</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Turn off AI prompts" id="disable-ai-prompts">
        <procedure title="Turn off prompt generation" id="turn-off-ai-prompts">
            <step>
                Go to <ui-path>Settings | Tools | Codecov</ui-path>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Clear <control>Enable AI prompt generation from coverage gutters</control> and click <control>OK</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
        <p>
            The <control>Generate AI Prompt</control> link stays in the coverage popup.
            When you click it, a notification reads "AI prompts are disabled. Enable them in Codecov settings."
        </p>
    </chapter>

